From: iPadOS-Cappu <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cappu: MT8176 touch driver (FocalTech FT5x46, I2C0 0x38), replaces Redmi GT9896

Full rationale, hardware facts (V) vs unverified bits (U), and the standalone
aarch64 compile check are in NOTES.md ("touch driver"/"cappu_touch_mt8176.c").
Short version: the Redmi driver (bsd/dev/cappu_touch.c) used Snapdragon GENI
I2C + SPMI PMIC keys, none of which exist on MT8176. This is a from-scratch
polling driver for the actual chip (FT5x46 over the MediaTek I2C0 block,
GPIO45/46 pinmux, FT5x06-family touch report). PMIC power/reset sequencing
for the touch rails is NOT done yet (documented in the driver header); if the
probe NACKs on real hardware, that is the first suspect. Also updates
CappuHID.cpp's hardcoded 1080x2436 (Redmi) panel geometry to the Mi Pad 3's
real 1536x2048 panel.

